<style>
  /* MTA route bullets: a circle for local service, a diamond for express.
     The feed names an express variant by suffixing X - 6X and 7X are the
     ones that run today - so the X is a shape, not part of the route name,
     and is stripped before display.

     Framework labels are pills, and it has no circle or diamond utility, so
     the two shapes are defined here. Sizes are in em so they follow whatever
     element size the label is given at each breakpoint; this block sets no
     font-size of its own. */
  .bullet {
    width: 1.7em;
    height: 1.7em;
    /* The framework's own .label padding lands later in the cascade and
       stretches the box back into a rounded rectangle once the glyph is
       two characters wide. Pinning min/max as well as width is what keeps
       SI a circle at the smaller layouts' label sizes. */
    min-width: 1.7em;
    max-width: 1.7em;
    padding: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .bullet--express {
    border-radius: 0;
    /* A rotated square's bounding box grows by root 2, so a diamond would sit
       29px wide beside a 20px circle and push its row out of line. Scaling by
       1/root 2 keeps the two occupying the same space. */
    transform: rotate(45deg) scale(0.707);
  }
  /* Counter-rotate the glyph so the number stays upright in the diamond. */
  .bullet--express > span {
    display: block;
    /* Undo both, so the glyph stays upright and full size in the diamond. */
    transform: rotate(-45deg) scale(1.414);
  }
  /* Two letters in a circle sized for one would touch the curve on both
     sides, so SI - the only two-character bullet in the system - is set
     smaller and tighter, which is what the MTA's own SI bullet does. The
     circle keeps its diameter, so it still lines up with every other
     bullet in the column. */
  .bullet--pair > span {
    /* 0.78em cleared the curve but rendered SI as a smudge in the smaller
       row labels on a 1-bit panel. 0.88em with the tracking pulled in is
       the most type that still fits, and stays legible at row size. */
    font-size: 0.88em;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    /* The circle's padding is zero, so without this the tracking on the
       final letter pushes SI visibly left of centre. */
    text-indent: -0.06em;
  }
</style>

{% comment %}
  Half the panel, wide and short — 800x240 on a TRMNL OG.

  The width still carries three columns, so the full board's structure holds;
  what changes is the vertical budget, which is roughly a third of the full
  layout's once the compact title bar is accounted for. Cards never split here:
  there is not room for two stacked lists plus their headings, so a column
  shows its top slot only and the bottom slot is simply not rendered.

  That is a deliberate loss rather than a scaled-down everything. A mashup cell
  is a glance, and four legible departures beat eight unreadable ones.
{% endcomment %}

{% assign device_height = trmnl.device.height | default: 480 %}
{% assign card_height = device_height | times: 30 | divided_by: 100 %}

<div class="view">
  <div class="layout">
    <div class="grid grid--cols-3 h--full">
      {% for column_index in (0..2) %}
        {% assign top_slot = column_index | times: 2 | plus: 1 %}
        <div class="col col--start gap--small">
          {% for card in c %}
            {% if card.s == top_slot %}
              <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--small">
                {% if card.b %}
                  {% for route in card.b %}
                    {% comment %}
                      The same rule the departure rows use: a bullet for one or two
                      characters, a pill for a named route, and the feed's X suffix
                      stripped because the diamond carries it.
                    {% endcomment %}
                    {% assign is_express = false %}
                    {% assign glyph = route %}
                    {% if route.size > 1 and route contains "X" %}
                      {% assign stripped = route | remove_last: "X" %}
                      {% if stripped.size == 1 %}
                        {% assign is_express = true %}
                        {% assign glyph = stripped %}
                      {% endif %}
                    {% endif %}
                    {% if glyph.size <= 2 %}
                      <span class="label label--small label--filled bullet{% if glyph.size == 2 %} bullet--pair{% endif %}{% if is_express %} bullet--express{% endif %}"><span>{{ glyph }}</span></span>
                    {% else %}
                      <span class="label label--small label--filled">{{ glyph }}</span>
                    {% endif %}
                  {% endfor %}
                {% endif %}
                <span class="title title--small grow" data-clamp="1">{{ card.n }}</span>
              </div>
              <div class="border--h-40 w--full"></div>

              {% if card.e %}
                <span class="label label--small label--outline">Unavailable</span>
              {% else %}
                <div class="content w--full"
                     data-content-limiter="true"
                     data-content-max-height="{{ card_height }}">
                  {% for col in card.k %}
                    {% for r in col.r %}
                      {% assign is_express = false %}
                      {% assign glyph = r[0] %}
                      {% if r[0].size > 1 and r[0] contains "X" %}
                        {% assign stripped = r[0] | remove_last: "X" %}
                        {% if stripped.size == 1 %}
                          {% assign is_express = true %}
                          {% assign glyph = stripped %}
                        {% endif %}
                      {% endif %}
                      {% if glyph.size <= 2 %}
                        {% assign bullet_class = "bullet" %}
                        {% if glyph.size == 2 %}{% assign bullet_class = "bullet bullet--pair" %}{% endif %}
                        {% if is_express %}{% assign bullet_class = "bullet bullet--express" %}{% endif %}
                      {% else %}
                        {% assign bullet_class = "" %}
                      {% endif %}
                            {% assign is_express = false %}
                      {% assign glyph = r[0] %}
                      {% if r[0].size > 1 and r[0] contains "X" %}
                        {% assign stripped = r[0] | remove_last: "X" %}
                        {% if stripped.size == 1 %}
                          {% assign is_express = true %}
                          {% assign glyph = stripped %}
                        {% endif %}
                      {% endif %}
                      {% if glyph.size <= 2 %}
                        {% assign bullet_class = "bullet" %}
                        {% if glyph.size == 2 %}{% assign bullet_class = "bullet bullet--pair" %}{% endif %}
                        {% if is_express %}{% assign bullet_class = "bullet bullet--express" %}{% endif %}
                      {% else %}
                        {% assign bullet_class = "" %}
                      {% endif %}
                {% if r[1] == r[0] %}{% assign destination = "" %}{% else %}{% assign destination = r[1] %}{% endif %}
                      <div class="flex flex--row flex--between flex--center-y gap--small">
                        <span class="label label--small label--filled {{ bullet_class }}">{% if bullet_class != "" %}<span>{{ glyph }}</span>{% else %}{{ r[0] }}{% endif %}</span>
                        {% if destination == blank %}
                          <span class="grow"></span>
                        {% else %}
                          <span class="title title--small grow" data-clamp="1">{{ destination }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                        <span class="title title--small">{{ r[2] }}</span>
                      </div>
                    {% endfor %}
                  {% endfor %}
                  {% assign total = 0 %}
                  {% for col in card.k %}{% assign total = total | plus: col.r.size %}{% endfor %}
                  {% if total == 0 %}
                    <span class="description">No upcoming departures</span>
                  {% endif %}
                </div>
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="title_bar">
    <span class="title">NYC Transit</span>
    {% if d %}
      {% comment %} Demo board; see the full layout for why this matters. {% endcomment %}
      <span class="instance">Example</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
